<title>UK: Sherwood &quot;cautiously optimistic&quot; for H2.</title>
<headline>Sherwood &quot;cautiously optimistic&quot; for H2.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British garment and lace manufacturer Sherwood Group Plc on Friday said it was &quot;cautiously optimistic of a gradual improvement&quot; in its markets for the second half of the current financial year.</p>
<p>Chairman David Parker told the company's annual general meeting there were signs of an improved performance in garments and while sales in the lace division began the year lower than the same period of 1996 there were indications the second half would show an improvement.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
